---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import QuestIcon from '../components/QuestIcon.astro';
import { data, href, fmt } from '../lib/data';
const weapons=data('weapons');
const chapters=data('chapters');
const skills=data('skills',{});
const featureLabels=['Industry','Magic','Exploration','Equipment','Moving machines','Homesteading'];
const picks=['simplyswords:whisperwind','simplyswords:stormbringer','epicfight:iron_dagger','simplyswords:bramblethorn','celestisynth:aquaflora','simplyswords:stars_edge'].map(id=>weapons.find((w:any)=>w.id===id)).filter(Boolean);
const professions=(skills.branches||[]).map((branch:any)=>({...branch,root:(skills.nodes||[]).find((node:any)=>node.root&&node.branch===branch.id)}));
const systems=[
 {id:'industry',icon:'rotation_mechanism',title:'A connected manufacturing path',body:'Create supplies the workshop’s mechanical backbone. Custom mechanisms connect its processing lines to Immersive Engineering, Applied Energistics 2 and later manufacturing stages. The next machine is a reason to improve the factory around it.',points:['Crafting, pressing, mixing and sequenced assembly serve different production jobs.','Recipe ingredients carry the progression requirements.','Digital storage and automated crafting become part of the same workshop.'],links:[['Explore the chapters','chapters/'],['Browse production recipes','recipes/']]},
 {id:'magic',icon:'bookred',title:'Several ways to practice magic',body:'Ars Nouveau, Iron’s Spells ’n Spellbooks and Witchery bring different tools to a magical character. Work with spellbooks, glyphs, rituals and magical materials, then connect the systems that support your preferred play.',points:['Resonant Arcana expands the spellbook side of the pack.','Spell scroll binding links school focuses, unfinished scrolls and ink.','Magical manufacturing meets the wider material and mechanism chains.'],links:[['Find magical systems','mods/#domain-1'],['Follow scroll binding','recipes/#family-spell-scroll-binding']]},
 {id:'adventure',icon:'map',title:'Exploration with useful discoveries',body:'Dungeons, structures and additional dimensions give expeditions a purpose beyond distance travelled. The Aether, The Twilight Forest and the End’s additions provide different places to explore, gather materials and prepare for demanding encounters.',points:['Encounter rewards feed equipment and crafting choices.','Boss materials and boss artifacts have their own uses.','A material toolset keeps its identity even when its material comes from an encounter.'],links:[['Explore boss encounters','bosses/'],['Browse the mod index','mods/']]},
 {id:'equipment',icon:'satchel',title:'A reward loop beyond the item name',body:'Unidentified Loot makes appraisal part of the return journey. Identify a find, compare its rarity and affixes with your build, then equip it or recover value through the salvage loop.',points:['Equipment tier, rarity and fighting style describe different properties.','Identification uses the experience and machine routes described in the equipment reference.','The Mechanical Identifier connects dungeon rewards to Create automation.'],links:[['Read the appraisal guide','loot/'],['See the custom systems','custom-mods/#unidentified-loot']]},
 {id:'moving-machines',icon:'rope',title:'Take engineering beyond a fixed base',body:'Aeronautics and Sable extend construction into moving contraptions. Let It Walk adds articulated walking machines, with the core, controls, joints and propulsion parts tied into the Reinforced stage of production.',points:['Walking-machine production shares Aeronautics’ Light Engineering stage.','Assembly chains retain the mod’s intermediate items and processing steps.','Combat Afloat connects Epic Fight interactions with Sable ships.'],links:[['Build a walking machine','guides/#walking-machines'],['Find Aeronautics recipes','recipes/?q=aeronautics']]},
 {id:'homesteading',icon:'herb',title:'Room for a quieter kind of progress',body:'Food, farming, storage and building systems support the place you return to between expeditions. Farmer’s Delight, Farm & Charm, Vinery and the pack’s decorative blocks give the workshop a home around it.',points:['Cooking and farming sit alongside other character activities.','Storage and logistics can grow with the size of a settlement.','Building, food production and exploration can develop alongside the main manufacturing path.'],links:[['Find farming and building mods','mods/'],['Start your first evening','guides/#first-steps']]}
];
---
<Layout title="Features" description="Explore the connected industry, combat, magic, character and exploration systems in Towns & Kingdoms.">
 <p class="eyebrow">Handbook / Features</p><h1>Industry, exploration<br />and character.</h1><p class="intro">Towns & Kingdoms brings a Create-centered workshop, distinct weapon styles and persistent character choices into the same world. Build a production line, prepare for an expedition or develop the place you call home.</p>
 <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Feature sections"><a href="#combat">Combat</a><a href="#character">Character</a>{systems.map((s,i)=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{featureLabels[i]}</a>)}</nav>
 <section id="combat" class="section feature-lead">
   <div class="section-heading">
     <div><p class="eyebrow">Combat / Epic Fight ecosystem</p><h2>Weapons with different jobs.</h2></div>
     <span class="tag">{fmt(weapons.length)} weapons & combat items</span>
   </div>
   <p class="feature-copy">Combat styles follow a weapon’s physical identity. Short daggers, thrusting swords, heavy blades, polearms and casting staffs use different handling; named artifacts add selected signature movesets. Compare the grip and style before choosing your next weapon.</p>
   <div class="button-row feature-weapon-links">
     {picks.map((weapon: any) => (
       <a class="button feature-weapon" href={href('weapons/#item=' + encodeURIComponent(weapon.id))}>
         <span class="feature-weapon-art"><img src={href(weapon.icon)} alt="" width="30" height="36" loading="lazy" /></span>
         <span class="feature-weapon-copy"><strong>{weapon.name}</strong><small>{weapon.styleName}</small></span>
       </a>
     ))}
   </div>
   <a class="button" href={href('weapons/')}>Compare weapon styles</a>
 </section>
 <section id="character" class="section feature-lead"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Character / Growth & identity</p><h2>Six professions, one connected tree.</h2></div><span class="tag">{fmt(skills.nodes?.length)} skills</span></div><p class="feature-copy">Earn character experience through play, choose an Origin and invest in the professions that support your interests. The skill tree connects six branches; you can plan across them while respecting each node’s requirements and the {skills.category?.pointCap||175}-point limit.</p><div class="feature-professions">{professions.map((branch:any)=><a href={href('skills/'+(branch.root?'#node='+encodeURIComponent(branch.root.id):''))}>{branch.root?.icon&&<img src={href(branch.root.icon)} alt="" width="35" height="35" loading="lazy" />}<span>{branch.title}</span></a>)}</div><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={href('skills/')}>Plan a skill build →</a><a class="button" href={href('mechanics/#origins')}>Explore Origins & ascension</a></div></section>
 <div class="feature-systems">{systems.map(s=><section id={s.id} class="feature-system"><div class="feature-system-title"><span class="card-icon"><QuestIcon name={s.icon} size={25} /></span><h2>{s.title}</h2></div><div class="feature-system-body"><p>{s.body}</p><ul>{s.points.map(point=><li>{point}</li>)}</ul><div class="feature-links">{s.links.map(([label,url])=><a href={href(url)}>{label} →</a>)}</div></div></section>)}</div>
 <section class="section"><div class="callout"><strong>Choose a starting point.</strong><p>The <a href={href('guides/')}>practical guides</a> introduce the first workshop, weapon handling and dungeon appraisal. The <a href={href('chapters/')}>{chapters.length}-chapter roadmap</a> explains how the manufacturing systems connect.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>
.feature-copy{color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;line-height:1.9;max-width:820px}.feature-lead{padding:28px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.feature-weapon-links{gap:8px;margin:20px 0}
.feature-weapon{justify-content:flex-start;padding:6px 12px;gap:8px}
.feature-weapon-art{width:30px;flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center}
.feature-weapon-art img{height:34px;object-fit:contain;image-rendering:pixelated}
.feature-weapon-copy{display:grid;gap:2px}
.feature-weapon-copy strong{font-size:14px;font-weight:550}
.feature-weapon-copy small{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px}
.feature-professions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px;margin:22px 0}.feature-professions a{overflow-wrap:anywhere;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:15px 6px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;background:var(--surface);font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.feature-professions a:hover{border-color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none}.feature-professions img{image-rendering:pixelated;object-fit:contain}.feature-system{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(210px,.8fr) minmax(0,1.4fr);gap:34px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:32px 0}.feature-system-title{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:14px}.feature-system-title h2{font-size:21px;margin:2px 0 0}.feature-system-title .card-icon{flex-shrink:0}.feature-system-body{color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;line-height:1.9}.feature-system-body p{margin-bottom:15px}.feature-system-body ul{margin:0 0 18px;padding-left:18px}.feature-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;font-size:14px}@media(max-width:1150px){.feature-professions{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.feature-system{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}}@media(max-width:520px){.feature-professions{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.section-heading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}.feature-system{padding:25px 0}.feature-system-title h2{font-size:20px}}
</style>
